  "knownLimitations": [
    "This exact-version desktop record applies only to Ubuntu x86_64. Windows and macOS remain protected by packed-install and platform CI rather than an equivalent 1.1.0-rc.2 live EasyEDA desktop record.",
    "The 2026-09-28 live-smoke report sampled bridge.hello immediately after BridgeManager.connect(); connect() starts the listener but does not wait for the extension handshake, so bridgeVersion could be absent even though later bridge calls passed. The reporter now waits for waitForConnection() before sampling hello. EasyEDA version was independently verified through the loopback-only desktop runtime identity because the extension handshake did not report it.",
    "At validation time, the checked-in EasyEDA 3.2.149 baseline used a legacy pre-schemaVersion format, so inventory:diff could not parse it directly; a bounded class/method comparison found zero drift. The baseline has now been refreshed from the same 2026-09-28 live capture to schemaVersion 1 with runtimePaths, and inventory:diff reports status=same across all 67 classes.",
    "EasyEDA Pro 3.2.149 PCB_PrimitivePolyline.modify is beta and, in this live run, returned the original id while replacing the disposable primitive with a new id. Cleanup therefore reconciled against the pre-mutation primitive-id inventory and removed the exact added replacement before accepting restoration.",
    "Concurrent host-side EasyEDA cache/WAL and warning-log activity changed aggregate ~/.config/EasyEDA-Pro and Documents/EasyEDA-Pro digests during the validation window. The validation namespace could not access those host paths; the host ~/EasyEDA-Pro project-data digest and installed easyeda-std.elib SHA-256 remained unchanged, and no host design project file was observed changed.",
